{
  "moduleId": "m00269",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00269:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Terpenoids"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "323f1800-5de3-4201-8424-000528bc7d37"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00269:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The structure of isopentenyl diphosphate is given in the box. The structure of four terpenoids named Camphor (monoterpenoid), patchouli alcohol (sesquiterpenoid), lanosterol (triterpenoid), and beta-carotene (tetraterpenoid)."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Thye condensation of (R)-mevalonate and 1-deoxy-D-xylose-5-phosphate leads to the formation of isopentenyl diphosphate (I P P). This further forms terpenoids."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "The Mevalonate Pathway to Isopentenyl Diphosphate"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00002-title",
            "text": "Step 1 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Claisen Condensation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "Claisen condensation of acetyl CoA and a thioacetate forms an intermediate that leads to the formation of acetoacetyl CoA."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 2 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Aldol Condensation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00269:caption:fig-00004-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "A four-step reaction is involved to produce isopentenyl diphosphate from acetyl CoA via acetoacetyl CoA adol condensation, (3 S)-3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl CoA reduction, and (R)-mevalonate phosphorylation."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Base catalyzed Aldol condensation of acetyl CoA with an enzyme-bound thiol diketone generated a tetrahedral intermediate which collapses to (3 S)-3-hydroxy-3-methylglutaryl coenzyme A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Step 3 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Reduction"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "H M G CoA is reduced by two nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride molecules to form an aldehyde intermediate and then (R)-mevalonate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00005",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00005-title",
            "text": "Step 4 of [[xref:fig-00004]]: Phosphorylation and Decarboxylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "(R)-Mevalonate reacts to form mevalonate-5-phosphate that further reacts to form mevalonate-5-diphosphate. Adenosine triphosphate converts to adenosine diphosphate. This forms isopentenyl diphosphate. Adenosine triphosphate converts to carbon dioxide."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00269:para:para-00010"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00269:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "Mevalonate-5-diphosphate reacts with two molecules of adenosine triphosphate to form mevalonate 5-diphosphate. Decarboxylation of the diphosphate phosphate forms isopentenyl diphosphate and carbon dioxide"
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_27_05_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00006",
      "class": "section-exercises",
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00269:title:sect-00006-title",
